\[
 \operatorname{ch}_3(V)
 ={1\over6}\bigl(c_1^3-3c_1c_2+3c_3\bigr).
\]

For `c1=0`, (6) implies `ch3=0` and therefore `c3=0` in real cohomology. This
contradicts (2), whose nonzero orientation class is part of the locked q79
visible physical character.

The obstruction is topological and independent of a numerical metric fit,
choice of spectral representative, or sign of the chiral branch. Both signs
in (2) are nonzero.

